# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Ouroboroid's beginning-of-combat trigger puts counters equal to its power on each controlled creature.
# Forcing: Advancing from Main1 is the only action needed and both creatures expose the exact counter result.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no permanents or decisions, so priority passes deterministically.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Both creatures gain one +1/+1 counter before attackers are declared.
#   LOSE = Combat advances without the expected power and toughness changes.
#   TIMEOUT = The phase trigger or its resolution fails to converge.
# Card roles:
#   Ouroboroid — source of the beginning-of-combat trigger and its power value.
#   Grizzly Bears — second recipient proving the effect applies to every controlled creature.
# Protocol path: Phase progression, triggered stack lifecycle, counter annotations, and refreshed object characteristics.

[metadata]
